 ],
 "notes": "CardDemo's user list (transaction CU00, program COUSR00C): a page of ten users browsed from USRSEC (STARTBR / READNEXT, ENDBR), PF8 / PF7 page forward and back from the page's last / first id (a READNEXT / READPREV first steps over the record the browse starts on), a 'U' or 'D' beside a user XCTLs to the update / delete screen. usrsec.txt is CardDemo's ten DUSRSECJ users plus fifteen synthetic ones (USER0006-USER0020, named for computing pioneers, written for this case) so that three pages exist. A defect of the original the case shows: a search past the last id makes STARTBR NOTFND, and the ENDBR that follows (no RESP) abends with INVREQ. Derived from CardDemo (Apache-2.0; Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates): LICENSE and NOTICE here are the source's own."
}
